# text = All the old sympathies of his sea-life strongly inclined him to follow Allan's suggestion ; but the wind was falling light , and he distrusted the broken water and the swirling currents of the channel ahead he said returned Allan Before Midwinter could answer , the current caught the boat , and swept them onward through the channel straight toward the wreck said Midwinter , quietly Both well accustomed to the use of the oar , they brought the course of the boat under sufficient control to keep her on the smoothest side of the channel -- the side which was nearest to the Islet of the Calf .
