# text = Thrice he stopped before he reached the stern end of the wreck : the first time , to throw aside his hat , and push back his hair from his forehead and temples ; the second time , reeling , giddy , to hold for a moment by a ring-bolt close at hand ; the last time ( though Allan was plainly visible a few yards ahead ), to look stealthily behind him , with the furtive scrutiny of a man who believes that other footsteps are following him in the dark he whispered to himself , with eyes that searched the empty air The stern end of the wreck was clear of the ship-breakers' lumber , accumulated in the other parts of the vessel .
