# text = He went back to Allan , sat down by his side , and took his hand he said , gently Before it was possible to reply , he snatched up the whisky flask from the deck he exclaimed , with a sudden effort to match his friend's cheerfulness Allan was delighted he said He sang the words of the glee in his old , cheerful voice , and clapped Midwinter on the shoulder in his old , hearty way returned Midwinter , contemptuously cried Allan For once Midwinter spoke as lightly and carelessly as Allan himself he said said Allan Midwinter trifled with his own superstition , as a man trifles with the loaded gun that may kill him , or with the savage animal that may maim him for life .
