# text = So revealed to all eyes that could read him aright , Major Milroy now stood before Allan , on the first morning of an acquaintance which was destined to be an event in Allan's life he said , speaking in the changeless quiet , subdued tone peculiar to most men whose occupations are of the solitary and monotonous kind replied Allan , delighted at his reception said the major he went on , changing the subject so abruptly that a closer observer than Allan might have suspected it was distasteful to him Miss Milroy's attention appeared to be already pre-engaged ; she made no reply .
