# text = He stood stiffly against the wall , like a man petrified , with one hand pressed on his bare head , and the other holding his hat -- he stood , with a dull flush on his face , and a dull stare in his eyes , looking straight into the black depths of the tunnel outside the station , as if the train to London had disappeared in it but the moment before asked the old gentleman Mr . Bashwood listened mechanically , with his usual attention , and answered mechanically , with his usual politeness he said , in a low , lost tone , like a man between dreaming and waking rejoined the old gentleman , making for the door Five minutes later , the porter charged with the business of locking up the station found Mr . Bashwood , still standing bare-headed against the wall , and still looking straight into the black depths of the tunnel , as if the train to London had disappeared in it but a moment since said the porter said Mr . Bashwood , answering the porter , exactly as he had answered the old gentleman
# sent_id = 4791
