# text = Bashwood the younger finished his breakfast slowly , out of pure bravado ; lit a cigar with the utmost deliberation ; looked at his father , and , seeing him still as immovably patient as ever , opened the black bag at last , and spread the papers on the table he asked said his father , eagerly He tapped his forehead smartly , and turned to the first page of the manuscript before him , with an unconcealed triumph at the prospect of exhibiting his own cleverness , which was the first expression of a genuine feeling of any sort that had escaped him yet said Bashwood the younger resumed Bashwood the younger , turning over the papers Bashwood the younger referred to the papers he replied asked Mr . Bashwood pursued Bashwood the younger He paused , and looked at his father in sudden perplexity .
