# text = In the box nearest the window two men were sitting talking together anxiously asked Bashwood the younger , suddenly joining them , and putting his question in a quick , peremptory whisper said one of the men , unwillingly said Bashwood the younger With those words , and with an oath to emphasize them , he left the coffee-shop and returned to the cab cried his father He fell back into his own corner of the cab , with a faint , wailing cry he moaned to himself ; his hands falling helplessly on his knees ; his hat falling unregarded from his head he exclaimed , suddenly rousing himself , and seizing his son in a frenzy by the collar of the coat shouted Bashwood the younger to the cabman he added , turning fiercely on his father
