# text = Mr . Bashwood , stealing up alone to the second floor to make his report , knew , the instant he set eyes on her , that the report was needless was all he said , as she slowly turned her head and looked at him She drew a long breath , and motioned him to be silent she said Turning from him at those words , she slowly paced the corridor to its furthest end ; turned , and slowly came back to him with frowning brow and drooping head -- with all the grace and beauty gone from her , but the inbred grace and beauty in the movement of her limbs she asked ; her mind far away from him , and her eyes looking at him vacantly as she put the question .
